; A price line without a date reads its commodity the way a dated price
; line does: quotes enclose the symbol and are not part of it, a quoted
; symbol may contain spaces, and a price that begins with a digit is not
; taken for a time of day.  `apply fixed` names its commodity the same
; way (#3321).

2025/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash                           100.00 USD
    Equity:Opening

P EUR 1.10 USD
P "N1" 2.00 USD
P "Fund A" 3.00 USD

apply fixed "Fund 2" 4.00 USD
2025/01/02 Buy
    Assets:Fund                           1 "Fund 2"
    Assets:Cash
end apply fixed

test pricedb --now 2030/06/15
P 2030/06/15 00:00:00 "Fund A" 3.00 USD
P 2030/06/15 00:00:00 "N1" 2.00 USD
P 2030/06/15 00:00:00 EUR 1.10 USD
end test

test print --now 2030/06/15
2025/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash                           100.00 USD
    Equity:Opening

2025/01/02 Buy
    Assets:Fund                         1 "Fund 2" {=4.00 USD}
    Assets:Cash
end test
